{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Split-hoofed [מפרסת].</b> A descriptive noun, likewise מקרין מפריס. The meaning: every animal that is described as having a hoof." "<b>And cleft-hoofed [ושוסעת שסע].</b> A descriptive noun. The meaning: its hooves are cloven." "<b>Chewing the cud [מעלת גרה].</b> From the root of גרון [throat], and מעלת is a participle. He mentioned the camel, the shafan, the arnevet, and the swine because each one has one of the two signs. The way of the holy tongue is to mention the masculine for every species, for the female is included in the masculine. He mentioned ארנבת — some say because the male of them is not found, and some say that the male turns into a female and vice versa, and the first opinion is closer to me."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:23.829650815Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}